From: Angel Martinez <110217098+anmartinez1256@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 22:24:36 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 01/39] Speed up the multithreaded engine on Apple M5
 (bit-identical to stock)

Combined tree: upstream gpu-engine plus the step-2 CPU work and this
session's items. All verified bit-identical to stock on the four bench
models (probes, S11/S21, nf2ff HDF5 dumps) and on the cylindrical
multigrid test; the GPU engine stays within 2.3e-4 dB.

- SpinBarrier (tools/spin_barrier.h) and a hook plan: extensions declare
  GetUsedHooks(), 44 -> few barriers per timestep (rebuilt when m_Eng_exts
  changes, so cylindrical multigrid stays correct).
- UpdateVoltages/Currents_IJKN inner loops, work stealing per x-line,
  slab balancing between threads.
- Fused sweep (Engine_Multithread::FusedTimestep): per x-line block V,
  V-hooks, then I of the line behind; Mur, UPML, excitation and lumped RLC
  gained *Lines() hooks. OPENEMS_FUSED=0 turns it off.
- Mur fast path on f4vectors: face cells per x-line in memory order,
  z-runs of x/y faces as vectors. UPML on f4vectors (full-z PML only).
- Field_Gather_SSE: dumps of the SSE engines use the precomputed gather
  with entry indices remapped to f4vector float offsets.
- numThreads=0: time IterateTS itself in short windows, balance slabs
  between probes, search P, P+2, .., max, P-2, then +-1 around the best.

MCells/s, stock v0.37.0 -> this tree (best thread count / auto):
  patch x5        1041 / 615 -> 1728 / 1655
  notch x3         845 / 534 -> 2007 / 1898
  patch tutorial   277 / 254 -> 1806 / 1444
  notch tutorial   318 / 247 -> 1470 / 1298

